- mcp_server.py (12): D:_mcp_gate@382-388, D:_resolve_http_runtime@426-436, D:compose_startup_opcert_binding@644-661, C:module@55-66, C:module@359-366, C:_readonly@393-397, C:build_server@511-515, C:build_server@545-559, C:build_server@567-573, C:build_server@611-623, C:main@676-679, C:main@711-713.\n- mirror_guard.py (3): D:replication_verdict@58-65, D:ruleset_verdict@85-91, D:_replication_check_with_lag_tolerance@204-210.\n- secret_screen.py (9): D:module@1-34, D:SecretFinding@121-126, D:iter_line_matches@148-153, D:_safe_segment@179-186, D:screen_event_data@194-201, D:override_record@218-223, C:module@53-55, C:module@58-72, C:module@92-100.\n- signing.py (11): D:module@1-22, D:verify_attestation_record@127-145, D:_sign_manifest_under_lock@171-176, D:_resolve_and_reduce@247-252, D:most_recent_attestation@282-291, D:_record_for_kind@301-305, D:verify_signature@313-324, D:verify_attestations@336-339, D:verify_signature_cli@395-405, C:module@69-73, C:module@111-114.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve MCP drain order and handshake; FastMCP tool names, schemas, force/gate semantics, and delivery fields; race-safe op-cert key custody, environment/principal binding, trust order, signed-subject replay defense, and authenticated material; immutable operation snapshots; process-group reaping and durable detached cwd; config exports/precedence/cache/tombstones; HTTP auth/stateless/proxy behavior; refuse-not-redact secret screening; and legacy/new signing dispatch. FastMCP consumes registered tool docstrings. The mcp_server module docstring is excluded because facade tests require its in-process-read statement; mirror_guard's module docstring is excluded because argparse publishes it.\n\nConcise/load-bearing prose outside the allowlist stays byte-identical. So do runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config values, and all 25 directive/shebang physical lines. All files are Python.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nParse base and final Python with `type_comments=True`; replace only allowlisted leading owner docstrings, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require the remaining AST/runtime tree to match. A zero-context base-to-final hunk guard restricts every deletion/insertion to an exact allowlisted base span. Run all six structured DD commands, including exact one-commit paths, focused consumers, scoped diff integrity, hygiene, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the patch records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 130 PASS rows, one per stable ID: `stable_id,before_citation,final_citation,preserved_contract_or_consumer,directives_exact,before_words,final_words,reviewer_session,semantic_pass,bloat_pass`. Every `final_words` is smaller; missing, extra, duplicate, or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 130 allowlisted blocks have smaller final word counts.\n- [ ] Non-allowlisted prose and all 25 directive/shebang lines remain exact.\n- [ ] The immutable-base runtime/non-comment oracle passes for every owned file.\n- [ ] Every preserved contract or consumer has an independent TSV PASS citation.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 11 declared paths and focused, diff-integrity, and hygiene checks exit 0.\n- [ ] Untimed worktree-venv `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788627021983397166,"uuid":"4edcae8f-1a13-4e61-8ec4-3bc9a9791786"}